item.description:
arXiv:2606.13373v2 Announce Type: replace-cross Abstract: Let $\mathcal{W}=\mathcal{W}_{n} oxtimes\mathcal{W}_{d-n}$ be a $d$-web on $(\mathbb{C}^2,0)$, where $\mathcal{W}_{n}$ is an $n$-web admitting an irreducible totally invariant curve $C$, and $\mathcal{W}_{d-n}$ is a regular $(d-n)$-web transverse to $C$. We show that the curvature of $\mathcal{W}$ is holomorphic along $C$ if and only if the curvature of $\mathcal{W}_{n}$ is. For each irreducible subweb $\mathcal{W}_{
u}$ of $\mathcal{W}_{n}$, we distinguish two cases depending on whether $C$ is strongly or weakly invariant by $\mathcal{W}_{
u}$; in the latter case, we introduce the 	extsc{Puiseux} index and exponent $\mathfrak{i}(\mathcal{W}_{
u},C)$ and $ho(\mathcal{W}_{
u},C).$ These invariants allow us to define the notion of non-degeneracy of $\mathcal{W}_{n}$ along $C.$ When $\mathcal{W}_{n}$ is non-degenerate along $C$, we prove that $K(\mathcal{W}_{n})$, and hence $K(\mathcal{W})$, is holomorphic along $C,$ generalizing a result of 	extsc{Mar'{\i}n} and 	extsc{Pereira}. Moreover, we obtain a natural decomposition of $\mathcal{W}_{n}$ as the product of two subwebs $\mathcal{W}_{n}=\mathcal{W}_{n}^{m{str}} oxtimes\mathcal{W}_{n}^{m{wk}}.$ Under the assumption that $\mathcal{W}_{n}^{m{wk}}$ is non-degenerate along $C$, we show that the holomorphy of $K(\mathcal{W})$ on $C$ is equivalent to that of $K(\mathcal{W}_{n}^{m{str}}).$ As an application, we establish a flatness result for products of dual webs of reduced convex foliations on $\mathbb{P}^{2}_{\mathbb{C}}$.
